;; Iraq (federal) public holidays 2019-2040: external gold for IQ.
;; Regenerate: uv run --no-project --with holidays==0.109 python -I scripts/generate_mena_holiday_gold.py IQ
;; :days lists every holiday as (YEAR MONTH DAY NAME); any other day is not one.
(
 :country "IQ"
 :generated "2026-11-28"
 :from 2019 :to 2040
 :note "Federal official holidays of Iraq: Law 110/1972 as amended to 27 May 2024 and the Official Holidays Law No. 12 of 2024 from then, with 3 October (Council of Ministers, 2020) and 10 December (2017), at the dates the Council of Ministers and its General Secretariat declared each year 2019-2026 (cabinet.iq, INA), with the Eid extensions. Kurdistan Region days, community-only days (25 December for Christians) and ad hoc closures (weather, Arbaeen, mourning) are left out. 2027-2040 are provisional: the statutory days and tabular estimates."
 :weekends ((nil 5) ((2005 2 26) 5 6))
 :sources
 (
  (:title "قانون العطلات الرسمية رقم (110) لسنة 1972" :uri "https://web.archive.org/web/20240820010527/https://wiki.dorar-aliraq.net/iraqilaws/law/5663.html"
   :text "Art.1 general holidays: Friday; Eid al-Fitr 3 days (1-3 Shawwal); Eid al-Adha 4 days (10-13 Dhu al-Hijja); 1 Muharram; Ashura 10 Muharram; Mawlid 12 Rabi I; 14 July; 17 July; 8 February; 6 January (Army Day); 21 March (Nowruz); 1 January; 1 May. Art.2 community-only days (Christians 25 Dec + 2 days of Easter; Jews; Sabians; Yazidis). Art.3 the President may declare temporary holidays for national occasions, max 7 days/year. No Arafah day. In force until 2024-05-27.")
  (:title "قانون تعديل قانون العطلات الرسمية رقم 110 لسنة 1972 (رقم 49 لسنة 1973، قرار مجلس قيادة الثورة 356)" :uri "https://web.archive.org/web/20250730080337/https://wiki.dorar-aliraq.net/iraqilaws/law/6165.html"
   :text "Replaces the Sabian community list only (2 days Great Feast, 1 day Little Feast, 2 days Feast of Creation, 1 day Prophet Yahya). No change to general holidays.")
  (:title "قرار مجلس قيادة الثورة رقم 886 في 12-7-1979: يوم 17 تموز العيد الوطني للجمهورية العراقية" :uri "https://wiki.dorar-aliraq.net/iraqilaws/law/12470.html"
   :text "17 July = national day (already a holiday under Law 110/1972); repeals RCC decision 856 of 22-11-1972. Repealed by Law 12/2024 art.4.")
  (:title "قرار مجلس قيادة الثورة رقم 210 لسنة 1989 (3 نيسان 1989): عيد التحرير 17 نيسان وعيد النصر 8 آب" :uri "https://wiki.dorar-aliraq.net/iraqilaws/law/14692.html"
   :text "17 April (Fao liberation) and 8 August (end of Iran-Iraq war) become annual official holidays. Abolished in practice by Governing Council decision 1/2003; formally repealed by Law 12/2024 art.4.")
  (:title "مرسوم جمهوري رقم 252 في 15-10-2002: اعتبار يوم 16 تشرين الأول 2002 عطلة رسمية" :uri "https://wiki.dorar-aliraq.net/iraqilaws/law/15827.html"
   :text "One-off holiday 2002-10-16 after the presidential referendum, under Law 110/1972 art.3.")
  (:title "قرار مجلس الحكم رقم (1) لسنة 2003 (first decision of the Iraqi Governing Council, 13 July 2003)" :uri "https://www.npr.org/2003/07/14/1337020/new-iraqi-governing-council-bans-saddam-holidays"
   :text "Abolishes six Ba'ath-era holidays: 8 Feb, 7 Apr (Ba'ath founding), 17 Apr, 28 Apr (Saddam's birthday), 17 Jul, 8 Aug; declares 9 April (fall of the regime) a national day and official holiday.")
  (:title "أمر رقم 18 لسنة 2005: تعديل الفقرة (1) من المادة الأولى من قانون العطلات الرسمية (الجمعة والسبت)" :uri "https://wiki.dorar-aliraq.net/iraqilaws/law/17148.html"
   :text "Weekend becomes Friday and Saturday (weekends handled elsewhere).")
  (:title "أمر رقم 25 لسنة 2005: اعتبار يوم 30 كانون الثاني عيداً وطنياً وعطلة رسمية من كل عام" :uri "https://wiki.dorar-aliraq.net/iraqilaws/law/17154.html"
   :text "Election day 30 January (2005 elections) = national day and official holiday every year. Repealed by Law 12/2024 art.4 (fourth). Observance 2006-2024 NOT verified (see IQ_OTHER_RULES).")
  (:title "إعلان رئيس الوزراء حيدر العبادي (9-10 كانون الأول 2017): 10 كانون الأول عطلة رسمية سنوية (يوم النصر)" :uri "https://www.newarab.com/news/iraq-marks-defeat-new-national-holiday"
   :text "10 December (victory over ISIS) declared an annual national holiday.")
  (:title "قرار مجلس الوزراء (24 كانون الأول 2018): 25 كانون الأول عطلة رسمية لجميع العراقيين ومشروع تعديل قانون العطل" :uri "https://www.kurdistan24.net/ar/story/292835"
   :text "Christmas (25 Dec) a holiday for all Iraqis in 2018; cabinet proposed amending the law. Not a standing rule: 2023 was Christians-only, 2022/2024/2025 general by yearly decision.")
  (:title "قرار مجلس الوزراء (1 أيلول 2020): 3 تشرين الأول من كل عام العيد الوطني لجمهورية العراق؛ إحالة مشروع قانون العيد الوطني الى مجلس النواب" :uri "https://www.iraq-businessnews.com/2020/09/03/cabinet-announces-another-public-holiday/"
   :text "3 October (admission to the League of Nations, 1932) = national day. Work suspended by yearly decision: 2021 (Sun), 2022 (Mon), 2023 (Tue), 2024 (Thu), 2026 (part of 30 Sep-3 Oct).")
  (:title "قانون العطلات الرسمية رقم (12) لسنة 2024" :uri "https://www.moj.gov.iq/upload/pdf/4777_453.pdf"
   :text "Art.1 first: general holidays: Fri+Sat; 1 Muharram; 10 Muharram (Ashura); 12 Rabi I (Mawlid); 1-3 Shawwal (Fitr); 10-13 Dhu al-Hijja (Adha); 18 Dhu al-Hijja (Ghadir); 1 Jan; 6 Jan (Army Day); 21 Mar (Nowruz); 1 May; 16 Mar (Ba'ath crimes: Halabja, Anfal, mass graves, Sha'baniya uprising). Art.1 second: first day of each Eid fixed by statement of the Shia and Sunni Endowment diwans; if they differ the holiday runs from the earlier first day to the later last day. Art.1 third: governorates with holy cities (Najaf, Karbala, Kadhimiya, Samarra) may close up to 3 days around religious holidays. Art.2 community-only days (Christians: Christmas + 2 days Easter; Sabians; Yazidis). Art.3: Council of Ministers may declare temporary holidays, max 7 days/year; may restore Saturday work. Art.4 repeals Law 110/1972, RCC 886/1979, RCC 210/1989, Governing Council decision 1/2003, Order 25/2005. NOT in the list: 14 July, 3 October, 10 December, 25 December (general), 9 April, Arafah.")
